@{
    ViewBag.Title = "About";
}
<h2>@ViewBag.Title</h2>
<p>@ViewBag.Message</p>

<p>This sample demonstrates a small but complete ecommerce flow:</p>
<ul>
    <li>A <strong>data-driven</strong> creature builder (creature types, option categories, options and colors all live in the database)</li>
    <li>Server-side <strong>price calculation</strong> from the selected options</li>
    <li>A session-based <strong>shopping cart</strong> and <strong>checkout</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Login and registration</strong> using Forms Authentication with salted PBKDF2 password hashing</li>
    <li>Persisted <strong>order history</strong></li>
</ul>

<div class="alert alert-info">
    <strong>Demo login:</strong> demo@example.com / Password123!<br />
    The database (including accounts) is recreated on every application start, so any accounts you register are reset each run.
</div>
